A||||5||RiceCooker||Monza Tips||||5||
Z||000000||RiceCooker||05-06-2000||10:12 PM||||Just a shot in the dark but does anyone else have the Monza dual exhaust chrome tips with reasonators? How do they sound? look?<BR>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||sluppy123||05-06-2000||10:49 PM||||I put a pair on my 85 2M4 about 3 years ago. I removed the muffler, made a custom y-pipe, and stuck 2 pairs of Monza's resonated tips on. They looked great, but after a few months the crome plating started peeling off and the yellow paint burned off, then they looked kinda' cheap. It sounded a lot better than the muffler(no more grand am sounding car) It's not overly loud. deep, throaty tone, not a high pitched ricey sound.  At certian RPM's the Harmonics would play games with your ears, Hwy driving, around 60, got really annoying.<P>Overall it looks and sounds good but not near as good as my GT's <B>GROWL</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>-Brian||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||05-07-2000||10:37 AM||||I had Hooker resonators (similar to Monza?) on my Formula, with no muffler. The thrum was *most uncomfortable*. Couldn't even carry on a converstion with the windows down. Ended up welding in a bullet glasspack, upstream from the Y-pipe. Sounds good, now.||||reg||1
Z||000003||zeusrekning||05-08-2000||09:46 PM||||I have a monza resonator tip on my 87 coupe People told me they could tell a difference when i got it but i really cant now. thinking of getting rid of cat converter b/c it has holes in it .||||reg||1
Z||000004||chris6878||05-09-2000||12:30 PM||||I just had an exhaust put on my car (v6)about 2 weeks ago. Had to order the muffler assembly at advanced auto because the guy at the muffler shop didnt have a clue what he was doing,    he says hes never seen nothing like it ...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">      well, i got the assembly, took it to him, he put at straight pipe in the area where the cat was and  put my stock tips back on. Its sound pretty good with no cat. Definetly better than it was, had a 3 inch hole in my muffler...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Now it has a slight rumble when ya give it gas...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">            ||||reg||3
Z||000005||87PegasusGT||05-09-2000||03:38 PM||||Had Monza's on my Camaro and Hot Tips on my GT (Same thing only red). I love them but they do look bad after a little wear.||||reg||1
